  "id": "60f78e8e-2755-5732-bfe0-5487cf697271",
  "slug": "tuna-melt-sliders-recipe-11892521",
  "name": "Tuna Melt Sliders",
  "recipe_type": "salad",
  "brief_description": "Try these tuna melt sliders, a warm, comforting twist on a classic tuna melt sandwich. The flavors are rich and savory, dominated by tangy tuna salad filling. Sharp Cheddar cheese adds a bold, melty saltiness. Hawaiian slider buns are soft, pillowy, and slightly sweet. The Dijon-garlic butter topping crisps the slider tops and adds an aromatic finish.",
  "cuisine": "American",
  "instructions": [
    {
      "position": 1,
      "text": "Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (180 degrees C). Lightly spray a 9x13-inch baking dish with cooking spray. Place bottom halves of rolls in the prepared baking dish, cut side up."
    },
    {
      "position": 2,
      "text": "Stir together tuna, celery, mayonnaise, relish, salt, and pepper in a bowl until evenly combined."
    },
    {
      "position": 3,
      "text": "Top rolls with 6 slices of Cheddar cheese, spread tuna mixture on top of the Cheddar, and cover with remaining 6 slices Cheddar."
    },
    {
      "position": 4,
      "text": "Place top halves of rolls on top, cut-side down. Stir together butter, Dijon, dill, and garlic until combined. Brush all but 1 1/2 tablespoons butter mixture evenly over the tops of rolls. Loosely cover rolls with aluminum foil."
    },
    {
      "position": 5,
      "text": "Bake in the preheated oven for 20 minutes. Remove and discard foil. Continue baking at 350 degrees F (180 degrees C) until cheese is completely melted, about 5 minutes more. Brush remaining butter mixture evenly over rolls. Serve immediately. Recipe developed by Amanda Holstein"
    }
  ],
  "servings": 5,
  "cooking_time_minutes": 25,
  "preparation_time_minutes": 15,
